        "original_id": "b1ff253c-6570-5618-a748-6fbc8892f5e0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Patrick McEnroe, Billie Jean King, Larry King, Boris Becker, Guy Forget, Jim Grabb\n- Roles: professional tennis players, Davis Cup captain, attorney, real estate broker, promoter, World Team Tennis founder\n- Organizations: United States Davis Cup team, World Team Tennis\n- Events: 1990 Newsweek Champions Cup – Doubles\n\nFacts:\n- Billie Jean King was born as Billie Jean Moffitt on November 22, 1943, and she became an American former World No. 1 professional tennis player.\n- Larry King was born on January 30, 1945, and he became an American attorney, real estate broker, promoter, and one of the founders of World Team Tennis.\n- Larry King was the former husband of tennis star Billie Jean King.\n- Patrick John McEnroe was born on July 1, 1966, and he became a former professional tennis player and the former captain of the United States Davis Cup team.\n- In the 1990 Newsweek Champions Cup – Doubles, Boris Becker and Guy Forget won the title by defeating Jim Grabb and Patrick McEnroe 4–6, 6–4, 6–3 in the final.",
